Click on tab didn't work? Likely an invisible element overlay? Let's inspect UI panel tabs event. It should call g.openPanel('hub', tab.dataset.tab). But `document.elementFromPoint` maybe click intercepted by panel body? The tab is at y=172. Could have clicked but no action. Maybe the `panelTabs` element not receiving because panel-body overlaps? Unclear. But actual click via playwright may have hit pseudo-element? It said page snapshot, click succeeded. Event listener should fire.

Maybe UI bind: `this.el.panelTabs.addEventListener('click', ...)` calls `g.openPanel('hub', tab.dataset.tab);`. Our `openPanel(tabId='command')` receives 'hub' as first arg and ignores second. Indeed! Game openPanel signature only one arg. UI calls `g.openPanel('hub', tab.dataset.tab)`, so tabId='hub', then UI.openPanel('hub') -> renderPanel('hub') -> defaults command. That's the bug. We need support both signature: `openPanel(typeOrTab, tabId)`. If first arg 'hub' or unknown, use second. Similarly UI's panel body data-tab same. Fix:
```
openPanel(tabId='command', maybeTab) {
  const tabs = ['command','weapons','recruit','supply','quests'];
  const actual = tabs.includes(tabId) ? tabId : (tabs.includes(maybeTab) ? maybeTab : 'command');
  ...
  this.ui.openPanel(actual)
}
```
Then g.openPanel('hub', 'weapons') works; our calls openPanel('quests') work. Good.

Also `UI.renderPanel(tabId)` if tabId 'hub' defaults command; we fix actual.

